oval — A candidate is kept or removed by decision, and its evidence is recorded before anything is removed\\\\n- [critical] sensei_code.derived.future_only_a_question_cannot_authorize_the_run_that_wrote_it — A derived question cannot authorize the run that wrote it\\\\n- [critical] sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope — Shared context explains why a change was asked for and never enlarges what may be changed\\\\n\\\\nArchitecture (components, boundaries, contracts, decisions, patterns):\\\\n- [decision] decision.sensei_code.prospective_authority_for_a_new_surface_existing_governed_fa — Prospective authority for a new surface: existing governed facts authorize a bounded CREATE operation, decided by a closed predicate, inspected after creation, never an anchor for a file that does not exist (sensei#312)\\\\n\\\\nGoverned synthesis loop available: for a repository Sensei has already onboarded (served graph authority, a task session, and closure state), golang/architecture/synthesisdriver can drive interpretation -\u003e plan -\u003e generation -\u003e evaluation -\u003e admission instead of ad hoc editing. Library only today, no CLI -- see docs/design/archer-integration-closure.md before assuming it is wired up for this task.\\\\n\\\\nInferred from this package (anchored to sibling files, NOT to this file):\\\\n- [decision] decision.sensei_code.fail_closed_when_claim_provenance_is_missing_or_outside_the — Fail closed when claim provenance is missing or outside the declared graph|repository|inference vocabulary.\\\\n  via internal/workflow/authority.go\\\\n- [failure_mode] failure.a_claimant_supplied_label_established_the_property_the_label — a claimant-supplied label established the property the label names\\\\n  via internal/workflow/authority.go\\\\n- [failure_mode critical] sensei_code.review_forked_the_conversation_it_was_judging — The reviewer was handed the architect's conversation and agreed with it\\\\n  via internal/workflow/adversarial.go\\\