{"id":"20260829T162547.674364308Z-402a4c7a","time":"2026-08-29T16:25:47.674364308Z","session_id":"session-20260829T161225.987217127Z","task_id":"task-1788019945987928256","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeXMMA192gNBbWTa1LpNy\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":361,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":170262,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":361},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"940b2d44-66f2-487c-ad1e-859b61bab5c1\",\"uuid\":\"b4cf0a22-886b-480d-85da-00f6e8e429f8\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T16:25:47.672Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeXMM95pXzwfngbA2ADk8\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
{"id":"20260829T162606.616050971Z-c9f911c7","time":"2026-08-29T16:26:06.616050971Z","session_id":"session-20260829T161225.987217127Z","task_id":"task-1788019945987928256","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeXMMA192gNBbWTa1LpNy\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. Full verification: `gofmt -l cmd internal` clean, `go vet ./...` clean, `go test ./...` passes except one pre-existing failure I confirmed at pristine HEAD (details below).\\n\\n## What I implemented\\n\\n**`internal/gitx/git.go`** — `Status`, `FileChange`, `ChangeSet`, `ChangeSet.Paths()` (both sides of a rename), `Repo.CandidateChanges` running `git --no-optional-locks diff --no-ext-diff --name-status -z \u003cbase\u003e --`, and `parseNameStatus` splitting on NUL, mapping `A/D/M/T/R`, sorting by path then old path. An unrecognised status letter is an error, not a guess.\\n\\n**`internal/report/report.go`** — `diffPath` now reads Git-quoted header sides (`splitQuotedHeader`, `quotedPrefix`, `headerName`, `headerValue`), and `rename from`/`rename to`/`+++` are unquoted the same way. `strconv.Unquote` handles Git's C escapes including three-digit octal. A token that will not unquote is kept verbatim rather than dropped, so the file stays visible and the mismatch surfaces at the reconciliation. Still a renderer, never authority.\\n\\n**`internal/workflow/engine.go`** — `authoritativeChanges` + `reconcileRenderedDiff` (package-level because `report` is shadowed by a local variable inside the cycle loop). Both binding points in `runCandidate` now obtain the ChangeSet, reconcile paths/status/rename-old-path, refuse naming the disagreement, and pass `changes.Paths()` to `confineToPlan`.\\n\\n**`internal/workflow/testedit.go`** — `confineToPlan(changed, planned)`, canonicalising with `path.Clean(strings.TrimSpace(f))`, naming every out-of-plan path, taking no grants.\\n\\n**Tests** — gitx: one real repo exercising non-ASCII, tab, quoted-old rename, quoted-new rename, quoted deletion, ASCII control, asserting statuses, both rename sides and parse order (it first checks Git still quotes, so it cannot silently stop proving anything). report: verbatim `git diff` output for that same change, plus the control-character case. engine: quoted out-of-plan modification, quoted out-of-plan deletion, rename whose old path is outside the plan, the four disagreement shapes, the in-plan candidate passing, both binding points in order ahead of every downstream consumer including the formatter-widening case, and one end-to-end test that `CandidateCapture`'s diff and `CandidateChanges` actually agree on a real candidate.\\n\\n## Three things you should know\\n\\n1. **`confineToPlan` did not exist.** The plan said to *change* it and to keep confinement \\\"still refusing at both binding points\\\" — there was no confinement anywhere in the repo. I added it with exactly the contract specified. This is therefore a new refusal in the governed path, not a rewiring of an existing one: candidates are now held to `tc.Files` where previously nothing did that.\\n\\n2. **A plan naming no files confines nothing** — `confineToPlan` returns nil for an empty `planned`. The plan did not say what an unscoped plan means, and the alternative (refuse every candidate) would break every run where the architect bounds a task without listing paths, which `renderScope` explicitly contemplates. Documented at the function. If you want the other reading, it is a one-line change and your call.\\n\\n3. **A Git typechange (`T`) will refuse.** I map `T` to `modified`, while `report.FromDiff` reads a typechange's `deleted file mode` + `new file mode` pair as `added` — so such a candidate hits the reconciliation refusal. That is the fail-closed direction and it is named in the error, but it is a real (rare) false refusal I did not repair, because repairing it means changing `FromDiff`'s status logic beyond the quoting fix you asked for.\\n\\nNot done, deliberately: no `sensei propose` entry for this failure class. Recording governance is outside the bounded plan — worth one if you want it.\\n\\nThe one failing test, `internal/publish.TestCommitAndPushReachARealRemote`, fails identically on a detached worktree at pristine `HEAD`: this candidate runs under a capability guard that denies `git push`, and that test needs a real push. Unrelated to this change.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/engine.go) | invariants: sensei_code.authority.only_an_explicit_answer_satisfies_a_boundary, sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope | uncertainty: preflight returned PREFLIGHT_STATUS_EMPTY with zero anchors over these files, so the confinement semantics for an unscoped plan and for a Git typechange rest on my reading rather than on graph evidence\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":361,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":170262,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":361},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"940b2d44-66f2-487c-ad1e-859b61bab5c1\",\"uuid\":\"b83b5a3c-546c-4e2f-94eb-a05948f115d5\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T16:26:06.605Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeXMM95pXzwfngbA2ADk8\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
