{"id":"20260829T162634.083340048Z-7fa6bc7d","time":"2026-08-29T16:26:34.083340048Z","session_id":"session-20260829T161225.987217127Z","task_id":"task-1788019945987928256","source":"reviewer","kind":"output","summary":"Add an authoritative changed-path source in internal/gitx/git.go: a ChangeSet type holding FileChange{Path, OldPath, Status} produced from `git diff --no-ext-diff --name-status -z` against the pinned base, parsed on NUL boundaries so no pathname Git can produce is lost or split, with both sides of a rename preserved and a deterministic order after parsing. In internal/workflow/engine.go, obtain that ChangeSet for the candidate and reconcile it against report.FromDiff(diff) at BOTH existing binding points -- the one immediately after the read-only (ModeInspect) refusal over the worker's diff, and the one immediately after e.validate returns over the diff validation re-read -- comparing the set of paths, each status, and rename old paths; if the two disagree in any of those, refuse the candidate the way the ModeInspect refusal does, naming the disagreement, before validation, the prospective inspection, the test-edit inspection, the audit, the Level-1 classification, the review or admission sees it. Confinement takes its paths from the authoritative ChangeSet rather than re-parsing the diff: change confineToPlan in internal/workflow/testedit.go to accept the changed paths (including rename old paths) and the plan's named files, canonicalising with path.Clean(strings.TrimSpace(f)) exactly as architecturalFiles does, refusing and naming every path outside the plan; it must not take or read test-edit grants. Repair internal/report/report.go so FromDiff parses Git-quoted headers (\"a/…\" and \"b/…\" with C-style escapes) and reports those files, because a report that silently drops a file is wrong regardless -- but it remains a renderer and never the source of pathname authority. Tests in internal/gitx/git_test.go: a non-ASCII path, a path containing a tab, a rename with a quoted old path and one with a quoted new path, a deletion of a quoted path, and an ordinary ASCII control, each appearing in ChangeSet with the right status and both rename sides. Tests in internal/report/report_test.go: FromDiff reports quoted and escaped paths, and the ASCII control still parses. Tests in internal/workflow/engine_test.go: a quoted out-of-plan modification is refused; a quoted out-of-plan deletion is refused; a rename whose old path is outside the plan is refused; a disagreement between report.FromDiff and the authoritative ChangeSet refuses before any downstream consumer; the ordinary in-plan candidate still passes; and confinement still refuses at both binding points, including a formatter that widens the candidate during validation. No other behaviour changes; no signature changes beyond confineToPlan's parameters; no new files.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
